---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

const siteUrl = (Astro.site ?? new URL('https://fknwine.com')).origin;

const aboutSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About FKN Wine',
  description:
    'FKN Wine — wine deals and honest buying guides. We check the fine print, we don\'t fake reviews.',
  url: `${siteUrl}/about/`,
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'FKN Wine',
    url: siteUrl,
    description: 'Wine deals, judged honestly. No sommelier act, no fake reviews.',
    foundingDate: '2026',
    slogan: 'F*ck Nice Wine.',
    contactPoint: {
      '@type': 'ContactPoint',
      contactType: 'customer support',
      email: SITE.email,
    },
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="What FKN Wine is and how we work: deals checked by hand, no fake reviews, opinions marked as opinions."
  articleSchema={aboutSchema}
>
  <section class="wrapper" style="padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 750px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem);">
      F*ck Nice <span style="color: var(--color-primary);">Wine.</span>
    </h1>

    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">
      Buying wine is annoying. The labels are noise, the prices are a lottery, and the people
      explaining it to you somehow always sound like they're selling something.
    </p>
    <p>
      FKN Wine exists to cut through that. We find wine deals that are actually good, read the
      fine print other sites skip, and tell you what's worth your money — in plain language,
      with dates and numbers.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-top: 2.5rem;">The rules we play by</h2>

    <div class="rule">
      <h3><Icon name="check-circle" size={18} color="var(--color-cta)" /> Deals are checked by hand</h3>
      <p>
        Before something lands on the deals page, we verify it on the merchant's own site and print
        the date we checked. Wine deals expire fast — the date tells you how fresh the page is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule">
      <h3><Icon name="check-circle" size={18} color="var(--color-cta)" /> No fake reviews</h3>
      <p>
        We don't invent tasting notes, we don't pretend we sipped something we didn't, and we don't
        run "10 best" lists pulled from thin air. When something is an opinion, it's marked as one.
        When it's a number, it comes from a source you can check. And when we haven't checked
        something, we say so — look for the "what we didn't check" notes in our reviews.
      </p>
      <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        The whole method is written down — what we read, what we refuse to fake, and where our
        knowledge stops: <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test a wine club</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule">
      <h3><Icon name="check-circle" size={18} color="var(--color-cta)" /> If it's not worth it, we say so</h3>
      <p>
        A wine club that's a bad deal for most people gets a bad verdict. A cheap bottle that
        punches above its price gets its flowers. We'd rather be useful than positive.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule">
      <h3><Icon name="check-circle" size={18} color="var(--color-cta)" /> Reader-supported, openly</h3>
      <p>
        FKN Wine is free to read. When we use links that earn us a commission, we say so —
        <a href="/disclosure/">the full disclosure is here</a>. Commissions never change the price
        you pay, and they never buy a verdict.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="brutal-card" style="margin-top: 2rem; border-color: var(--color-cta); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 0 var(--color-cta);">
      <p style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; text-transform: uppercase;">No one's palate is wrong.</p>
      <p style="margin: 0.35rem 0 0;">
        If you like it, it's good. We're just here to make sure you don't overpay for it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-top: 2.5rem;">Who's behind this</h2>
    <p>
      A tiny independent operation from Bochum, Germany — obsessed with wine value, allergic to
      snobbery. Not a publisher with a tasting panel, not a merchant: two people, a spreadsheet of
      fine print, and a rule that we publish the date we checked and the things we could not verify.
    </p>
    <p>
      We write under the name FKN Wine rather than a personal byline. That's a deliberate choice, and
      we'd rather tell you why than let you guess: this site is meant to be judged by its paperwork —
      the prices, the terms, the dates — not by a personality. Who is legally responsible for the
      site is a matter of public record in the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a>, and the email on this
      page reaches a human.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or on
      <a href={SITE.x} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X (@FKNWine)</a>. Got a term we read
      wrong? Say so and we'll check it against the source.
    </p>

    <div class="brutal-card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <p style="margin: 0;">
        <strong>21+ only.</strong> We write about wine; we don't sell it. Every merchant we link
        to runs its own age checks and handles its own shipping rules — as it should be.
        Enjoy responsibly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;">
      <Icon name="wine" size={20} color="var(--color-primary)" /> F*ck Nice Wine.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .rule {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .rule h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .rule p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
